\viewkind4\uc1\pard\f0\fs26\b Tech Bench quick reference\b0\fs20\par
\par
\b Keyboard shortcuts\b0\par
F1\tab Open this cheat sheet (press F1 again to focus it if it is already open)\par
Ctrl+F or F3\tab Jump to the search box on the Search page\par
Ctrl+N\tab Add a fault code to the knowledge base\par
Enter (in search)\tab Run search now\par
Down (in search)\tab Move focus into the results list\par
\par
\b Main navigation\b0\par
Search\tab Fault codes, manuals, rental filters/oil, equipment, iFix passwords, shop notes and files\par
Work orders\tab Pick a WO, notes, photos, INLINE 7 shots, diagnostic report, shop share, IntelliDealer log on/off when configured\par
INLINE 7\tab Cummins INLINE 7 / J1939: connect, live data, codes, trend, timeline, unit history, report, bus monitor\par
Adapters\tab RP1210 adapter list and whether this process is 32-bit (required for INLINE 7)\par
\par
\b Job strip (top)\b0\par
WO picker\tab Load customer, model, and serial from a work order\par
Search this job\tab Search using model and serial from the strip\par
Add code to KB / Add note\tab Same as Ctrl+N and Shop - Add note\par
Sync line\tab Click for Shop sync status and settings\par
\par
\b Shop menu\b0\par
Sync now / Sync...\tab Two-way share of shop notes, user codes, and files through the KB or a folder you pick\par
Add note / Add file...\tab Drop a text note or copy a file into the knowledge-base shop folder\par
IntelliDealer settings\tab Azure API Gateway credentials (DPAPI-protected, not in the repo)\par
Refresh work orders\tab Reload the assigned work-order list\par
\par
\b Help menu\b0\par
Check for updates\tab Read latest.json and a hashed TechBench.exe (applies after you quit, never mid-session)\par
Install update\tab Enabled when a verified update is staged\par
About Tech Bench\tab Version, install path, knowledge-base location, process bitness\par
\par
\b Search filters (kind box)\b0\par
ALL, CODE, PASSWORD, MANUAL, FILTER, EQUIP, NOTE, FILE\tab Narrow what the index searches\par
\par
\b INLINE 7 (high level)\b0\par
Connect\tab Close USB-Link 3 Explorer and Guidanz first so the adapter is not locked\par
Module box\tab Whose DM1/DM2 the code lists show (engine vs compressor controller, etc.)\par
Reset / clear codes\tab J1939 DM11/DM3 requests with per-module report; no DEF/SCR disable or calibration writes\par
Trend / Timeline / Unit history\tab Session charts and fleet history from saved _dtcs.csv files\par
Report\tab Printable one-page summary for the current work order\par
Sessions\tab Saved under Desktop\\TechBench-sessions (or Documents / LocalAppData fallback)\par
\par
\b Knowledge base\b0\par
Shipped data is embedded in TechBench.exe and copied beside the exe on install. Override with TECHBENCH_KB, kb-path.txt, or sync-path.txt next to the exe.\par
}
